{
  "_about": "Every file that still puts a roll on record by hand, outside the one door for it (src/lib/dm/roll-record.ts recordRoll): how many times it stores one (insertRoll), sends one (a publish of \"roll_result\") and adds one to a turn's cards (a push or other write onto rollIds, or joinStoredTurn), and the family of sites it moves onto the door with. A site moved is struck off, so the counts only go down; `total` is their sum. A send through a file's own wrapper is counted once, where the wrapper is written; a new site in such a file still shows, because it has to store its roll. Held by scripts/test-roll-record-sites.mjs; `node scripts/test-roll-record-sites.mjs --counts` prints what the source holds now.",
  "total": { "store": 20, "send": 19, "join": 2 },
  "families": {
    "opportunity": "An opportunity attack's swing and damage, made on a stand-in turn that nothing draws its cards from.",
    "clock": "Dice rolled as time passes or a rest is taken, with no GM call around them: death saves and the stable timer, hit dice, an item's charges. Death saves post a line of their own, which is their card's home.",
    "initiative": "The dice that open a fight. Creatures' initiative and stealth are stored for the GM and handed no turn; by the ruling on issue #915 they join the turn as a creature's saves do.",
    "requests": "A roll a person asked for outright (the dice tray, the GM's roll table), a parked roll put on record as it lands, and a secret roll sent again once it comes out."
  },
